    "body": "## Motivation\n\nIn `python/sglang/srt/eplb/eplb_algorithms/deepseek_vec.py`, `pack_groups()` previously executed per-item 0-D PyTorch tensor operations (`full.masked_fill_`, `argmin()`, tensor indexing, and in-place scalar writes) inside the nested `num_layers * num_groups` greedy packing loop:\n\n```python\nfor i in range(num_layers):\n    pack_weights = torch.zeros(num_nodes, device=device, dtype=torch.int64)\n    pack_items = torch.zeros(num_nodes, device=device, dtype=torch.int64)\n    full = torch.zeros(num_nodes, device=device, dtype=torch.bool)\n    for group in indices[i]:\n        full.masked_fill_(pack_items >= groups_per_node, True)\n        pack = pack_weights.masked_fill(full, float(\"inf\")).argmin()\n        ...\n```\n\nWhile `deepseek.py`'s `balanced_packing` was optimized in #21232 to convert tensors to Python lists before running the greedy loop, `deepseek_vec.py`'s `pack_groups` still ran 8–10 PyTorch dispatcher launches per `(layer, group)` iteration. For a DeepSeek-V3-scale configuration (`num_layers=60`, `num_groups=256`, `num_nodes=8` = 15,360 iterations), `pack_groups` spent ~2.0 seconds in Python/ATen dispatch overhead per rebalance call.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Convert sorted `indices` (`indices.tolist()`) and `tokens_per_group` (`tokens_per_group.tolist()`) to Python lists once before the loop in `deepseek_vec.pack_groups`.\n- Perform the greedy bin-packing loop (`min(range(num_nodes), key=...)` and weight/count updates) in pure Python lists and construct `pack_index` and `rank_in_pack` in a single `torch.tensor(..., dtype=torch.int64, device=device)` transfer at the end.\n- Add `TestPackGroups` unit test in `test/registered/unit/eplb/test_balanced_packing.py` verifying slot uniqueness, bounds, and exact match with `deepseek.balanced_packing`.\n\n## Benchmark\n\nMeasured on CPU across 20 runs (`torch.manual_seed(42)`):\n\n| Shape `(num_layers, num_groups, num_nodes)` | Before (`ms`) | After (`ms`) | Speedup |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `(58, 8, 2)` | 59.8 ms | 0.9 ms | **66.9x** |\n| `(60, 64, 8)` | 495.3 ms | 6.5 ms | **76.2x** |\n| `(60, 256, 8)` | 2,003.8 ms | 25.8 ms | **77.7x** |\n\nOutputs (`pack_index`, `rank_in_pack`) are bit-for-bit identical before and after.\n\n## Community Credit & Acknowledgments\n\n- Credits to @bixue2010 for the list-conversion optimization in `deepseek.balanced_packing` (#21232) and @DarkSharpness for the vectorized EPLB implementation in `deepseek_vec.py` (#18850).\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format code and run unit tests (`pytest test/registered/unit/eplb/test_balanced_packing.py -v` — 11 passed)\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:warning: [Run #41258542440](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41258542440)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:warning: [Run #41258542411](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41258542411)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:warning: [Run #41258542399](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41258542399)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
